# Plotmaniac aesthetic

Treat the current coming-soon page as the visual source of truth. Future pages, components, and restyles must stay in line with it unless the user explicitly asks for a different look.

Do not invent a second visual system. Do not “modernize,” brighten, or add a generic SaaS/marketing UI.

## Palette

Use only these tokens from `styles.css`:

- Background: `--bg` `#0c0b09` (warm near-black)
- Ink: `--ink` `#f4efe6` (warm off-white)
- Muted copy: `--muted` `#9b9488`
- Accent: `--gold` `#e8c47a` (labels, rules, marks, focus)
- Grid lines: `--line` `rgba(244, 239, 230, 0.12)`

No pure white, no cold gray, no saturated brand colors, no large color blocks.

## Type

- Display / titles: Fraunces, weight 500, tight tracking (`-0.04em`), tight line-height.
- UI, labels, body: IBM Plex Mono.
- Eyebrows / kicker text (`.status`): gold, ~0.72rem, uppercase, `0.28em` letter-spacing.
- Body / lede: muted, ~0.92rem, `1.7` line-height, measure around `42ch`.

Do not switch to Inter, Geist, system UI sans, or heavy bold display type.

## Surface and layout

- Keep the faint 72px grid overlay that fades out toward the edges (`body::before` in `styles.css`).
- Generous empty space. Centered, calm compositions. Avoid dense cards, heavy borders, drop shadows, glassmorphism, and rainbow gradients.
- Hairline gold strokes and small gold dots are the right kind of decoration. The story-arc mark is part of the identity; reuse that language rather than adding new ornaments.
- Content width stays modest. Prefer a single column over dashboards.

## Motion

- Sparse and slow. Line-draw / fade-in only, similar to the existing 1.8s arc.
- Always honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Implementation

- Put shared look in `styles.css`. Add page-specific layout there or in a small extra stylesheet; do not fork new color or font tokens.
- Load Fraunces and IBM Plex Mono the same way the coming-soon page does.
- Keep `favicon.svg` as the gold arc on warm black.

Reference: `index.html` + `styles.css`.
